KZ3 patch 4027 (network pass 45): the Keyboard page's own text in the game's language. The page lines the pad library
builds (the idle hint "Enter change, Delete clear, ...", the capture / timeout / conflict status, the labels of the rows
the game has no word for: the eight stick directions, Pause, Back) go through PAD_KB_TR(key, en): cellPad.c points it
at g_pad_kb_tr, which port/net/kz3_discord.c sets to the port's lookup (port/net/kz3_tr.h kz3_tr, keys kb.* of
port/text/port_ui.tsv); NULL or any other includer of pad_keybinds.h keeps the English text. {0}..{2} are filled by
pad_kb_fmt (the lookup refuses a translation whose placeholders differ from the English text's).

--- a/libs/input/cellPad.c
+++ b/libs/input/cellPad.c
@@ -22,6 +22,12 @@
 #include "pad_menu_mouse.h"
 #include "pad_mouse.h"
 #include "pad_kbport.h"   /* KZ3 patch 4026 */
+
+/* KZ3 patch 4027 (network pass 45): the Keyboard page's own text in the game's language through the port's lookup
+ * (port/net/kz3_tr.h kz3_tr, set by port/net/kz3_discord.c at start); NULL = English. Before every include of
+ * pad_keybinds.h (POSIX and Windows paths below). */
+const char* (*g_pad_kb_tr)(const char* key, const char* en) = NULL;
+#define PAD_KB_TR(key, en) (g_pad_kb_tr ? g_pad_kb_tr((key), (en)) : (en))
 unsigned (*g_pad_menu_bits_hook)(unsigned pad_buttons, int pad_active) = NULL;
 /* KZ3 patch 2106: a game menu has the focus, so the "back" keys (Esc) are menu Back (pad_keybinds.h pad_kb_eval). Only
  * when the port tracks the game's menus (2098's hook installed: a GUM context was found for this EBOOT); otherwise
